.idea/
.env/
# Work-in-progress notes, issue drafts and design docs live in the sibling repository
# `tools-agent-tools-restricted-wip`. This directory holds only an untracked pointer to it
# (wip/CLAUDE.md), and the tracked files do not reference any path under it.
wip/
# Compiled policy packages are build artifacts and are not committed: the RPM build compiles
# every shipped module against the building distribution's policy headers, and a source install
# compiles the same set from the checkout (selinux/policy/shipped-modules.sh derives which). A
# .pp is a binary no review can read, so tests/unit/selinux-groups.sh fails on a tracked one.
# The refpolicy build scratch under tmp/ goes with them.
selinux/policy/*.pp
selinux/policy/tmp/
selinux/avc/.avc-last-run
selinux/avc/audits/
.avc-scratch/
ai_tools_exec_t
# Self-cleaning fixture dir from tests/integration/hooks.sh (left only if a run is killed).
.handback-test.*

# Python bytecode cache -- created next to the handback daemon/client when they are run or
# imported (e.g. a test loading the daemon); never a source artifact.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Emacs backup and lock files
*~
.#*

# Per-user Claude Code permission grants written by the harness; never shipped
.claude/settings.local.json
